{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774312771,"nonce":"suyzlTPu84k+EHrH3haDQ0HmuO4=","message":"## Implementation Spec\n\n### 1. Types (web/src/types/analysis.ts)\n\nNew types:\n\n```typescript\n// Viewport state for an analysis page\ninterface AnalysisViewport { x: number; y: number; zoom: number }\n\n// Eval parametrization — extensible dict for now\ninterface EvalParametrization { [key: string]: unknown }\n\n// Persisted spec for a single analysis page\ninterface AnalysisPageSpec {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  graphSpec: AnalysisGraphSpec;\n  evalParams: EvalParametrization;\n  viewport: AnalysisViewport;\n}\n\n// Snapshot of ALL analysis state (used by projectsStore)\ninterface AnalysisSnapshot {\n  pages: AnalysisPageSpec[];\n  activePageId: string | null;\n}\n```\n\n### 2. analysisStore (web/src/stores/analysisStore.ts)\n\nAdd multi-page state:\n- `pages: AnalysisPageSpec[]` — list of saved page specs\n- `activePageId: string | null` — which page is currently loaded into the React Flow state\n- `viewport: AnalysisViewport` — current viewport (not tracked by React Flow store directly)\n- `evalParams: EvalParametrization` — current eval params\n\nActions:\n- `addPage(name)` — create new blank page, switch to it\n- `removePage(id)` — remove a page; if active, switch to adjacent\n- `renamePage(id, name)` — rename a page\n- `switchPage(id)` — capture current page state into pages[], restore target\n- `setViewport(v)` — update viewport\n- `setEvalParams(p)` — update eval params\n- `captureSnapshot(): AnalysisSnapshot` — snapshot all pages + active page (capturing current active into its slot first)\n- `restoreSnapshot(snapshot)` — restore all pages and load active page into React Flow state\n- `resetAnalysis()` — clear all pages and state\n\n### 3. projectsStore (web/src/stores/projectsStore.ts)\n\n- Add `analysisSnapshot: AnalysisSnapshot | null` to `OpenTab`\n- `captureGraphSnapshot` helper unmodified; create parallel `captureAnalysisSnapshot()` wrapper\n- In every place where graph + training snapshots are captured/restored (openNewTab, openProjectInTab, switchTab, closeTab), also capture/restore analysis snapshot via `useAnalysisStore`\n- New helper `resetAnalysisStoreForTabSwitch()` for non-snapshot tab switches\n\n### 4. Backend (feedbax/web/models/graph.py)\n\nNew Pydantic model:\n```python\nclass AnalysisPageSpec(BaseModel):\n    id: str\n    name: str\n    graph_spec: Dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n    eval_params: Dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n    viewport: Dict[str, float] = Field(default_factory=lambda: {'x': 0, 'y': 0, 'zoom': 1})\n```\n\nExtend `GraphProject`:\n```python\nanalysis_pages: Optional[List[AnalysisPageSpec]] = None\n```\n\n### 5. Backend service + API\n\ngraph_service.py `update_graph` — add optional `analysis_pages` param, persist alongside graph+ui_state.\ngraphs.py `GraphUpdateRequest` — add `analysis_pages: Optional[List[AnalysisPageSpec]] = None`.\nGET endpoint returns `analysis_pages` from project.\n\n### 6. Frontend API (web/src/api/client.ts + analysisAPI.ts)\n\n- Extend `updateGraph()` to accept optional `analysis_pages` param\n- Extend `fetchGraph()` response type to include `analysis_pages`\n- Wire `saveAnalysisGraph` and `fetchAnalysisGraph` in analysisAPI.ts to use real graph endpoints\n\n### 7. Auto-save (App.tsx)\n\n- Subscribe to analysis store dirty state alongside graphStore dirty\n- Include `analysis_pages` in the auto-save payload when saving\n- Analysis mutations mark graphStore as dirty (analysis rides on the same dirty/save cycle)\n\n### Design decisions:\n- Analysis pages are stored as an optional field on GraphProject for backward compat\n- No separate endpoint — analysis_pages travel with the graph PUT/GET\n- EvalParametrization is a freeform dict now, constrained later\n- Viewport stored per-page so switching pages restores scroll/zoom position\n- The existing analysisStore single-graph state becomes the active page materialization","files":null}]}